From d05beafc3b274bef46314334ee4faec661c8fcd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenSec <contactus@opensec.in>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:04:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Ahead-of-time compiled executables: static heap, code image,
 x86-64

`bun build --compile --bytecode --format=esm` with BUN_STATIC_HEAP=1 and
BUN_AOT=1 compiles every function of the program ahead of time and appends a
prebuilt heap and a code image to the executable, which maps both at a fixed
address on start.

- Image trailer (BAOTIMG3) with the CPU features the code was compiled for and
  the engine options it takes for granted; BUN_AOT_CPU=baseline compiles for
  any x86-64 CPU Bun's baseline build runs on; BUN_AOT_JIT=0 bakes "run with
  the JIT off" into the executable.
- The image is mapped before the heap, and neither is used unless both fit:
  a CPU without a required feature, an address space limit, a taken address
  or an image the engine rejects falls back to the program's bytecode, with a
  one-line notice. BUN_AOT=0 is the kill switch.
- The builder runs with the JIT off itself (what the JIT records in cells is
  not what the program finds when it runs); a build that cannot honour
  BUN_STATIC_HEAP=1 fails instead of silently producing a plain executable.
- Workers share the static heap (prepareThread() at thread start).
- Prelinked module graph v4 plumbing; JSType numbers of the AOT engine.
- Local WebKit builds against a Linux sysroot (LINUX_GLIBC_SYSROOT), with
  ICU from the sysroot, for portable release builds.
